        "execSummary":  "Vera\u0027s general availability marks the arrival of purpose-built silicon for the agent orchestration layer — a signal that agentic AI is no longer a prototype workload but a first-class infrastructure concern. For enterprise technology leaders, the key implication is that agent performance and economics will increasingly depend on hardware choices, not just model selection or prompt engineering. The adoption by Anthropic and OpenAI as early recipients validates the architecture, but enterprises procuring cloud capacity should ask providers whether their AI services run on Vera or commodity x86, as this will affect latency and throughput for orchestration-heavy agent pipelines. This also reinforces NVIDIA\u0027s strategy of owning the full AI stack from chip to software, which has long-term vendor concentration implications.",
