        "title":  "Deloitte aims to help enterprises with hybrid AI model strategy",
        "source":  "CIO Dive",
        "url":  "https://www.ciodive.com/news/Deloitte-open-source-models-practice-engineering/829722/",
        "date":  "2026-09-04",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Deloitte launched an Open Model Engineering practice to help enterprises balance proprietary and open-source AI models as they build technology stacks. The service deploys specialized forward-deployed engineers through 2027 across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific to help organizations optimize technical choices and maximize ROI while maintaining flexibility in AI infrastructure.",
        "execSummary":  "Deloitte is productizing the hybrid AI model question — proprietary vs. open-source — that virtually every enterprise is wrestling with right now, deploying dedicated engineers to sit inside client environments and optimize those tradeoffs in real time. For enterprise AI leaders, this signals that the market now has a named service for a problem many are solving ad hoc, which raises the bar for internal capability. The strategic implication is clear: if you don\u0027t have a deliberate model-selection framework, a competitor may gain cost or performance advantages through better mix optimization. Watch whether other Big Four firms launch competing practices, which would accelerate pricing pressure and open new procurement options.",
