        "title":  "Fewer than 25% of enterprises have scaled AI successfully",
        "source":  "CIO Dive",
        "url":  "https://www.ciodive.com/news/rising-spend-cios-AI-success/829484/",
        "date":  "2026-09-02",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "Gartner\u0027s survey of over 1,300 organizational leaders found that fewer than one-quarter of enterprises have successfully scaled AI across multiple business units. Despite 85% of tech leaders planning increased AI investments, many organizations struggle with measuring ROI and knowing when to discontinue underperforming AI initiatives.",
        "execSummary":  "Gartner\u0027s data points to a widening execution gap: enterprises are spending more on AI while scaling it successfully less than a quarter of the time, suggesting the bottleneck has shifted from adoption to operationalization. For senior leaders, this reframes the strategic question from \u0027are we investing in AI?\u0027 to \u0027do we have the governance, measurement, and portfolio-management discipline to scale it?\u0027 The ROI measurement gap is particularly acute — organizations that cannot quantify what working looks like also cannot identify what failing looks like early enough to cut losses. The implication is that AI portfolio management, including explicit kill criteria for projects, is now a core enterprise capability gap to address.",
        "vendorLean":  "Neutral — data sourced from Gartner research; no vendor promoted",
